	(wire (pts (xy 35.56 25.4) (xy 35.56 27.94)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "02d35a6e-c2d5-4264-9045-d3280f0ddbe2"))
	(label "XIAO_5V" (at 35.56 27.94 270) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "1a251b23-e301-4b19-b09c-a43251d47e95"))
	(text "XIAO pads, USB-C up, from the top: left D0 D1 D2 D3 D4 D5 D6, right 5V GND 3V3 D10 D9 D8 D7;\nBAT+ and BAT- on the back. The microSD of the Sense board takes D8 CLK, D9 DAT0, D10 CMD and\nGPIO21 for DAT3, inside: leave D8-D10 free. D1 is spare, for the optional aux channel." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 193.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "965f0e24-4564-455e-bf85-08c6317fd1d2"))
	(text "Keys: the JS5208's centre pulls D0 to ground; each direction does so through its resistor,\nagainst the 10 k pull-up: about 0.6, 1.05, 1.65 and 2.27 V (PLAN-ESP32.md 3.1).\nThe IMU shares the I2C bus with the display; the GM10 runs from the buck's 5 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6bdd3cd3-f69e-4901-b135-e51fc2cbbfda"))
	(text "RC front end: the buffer takes 3.3 V or 5 V logic and gives D2 and D3 a clean 3.3 V; the\n100 k pull-downs hold its inputs low with the receiver off, as the RC inputs wake the chip." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 236.22 190.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ca59ee3a-abd9-49f2-af0f-25db8ab3e570"))
	(text "Power: never the receiver rail straight into the 5V pad. D1 guards against reverse polarity,\nC1 and C2 soak up the servo's spikes, and the buck holds 5 V from 5 to 8.4 V in. D2 keeps\nthe car's 5 V and the USB's apart: to confirm against the XIAO's schematic, which may already\nisolate VBUS. The LiPo on the BAT pads carries the shutdown when the car is switched off." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ebe46039-22f6-44f0-b2d7-d62ba29f6b2d"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))) (embedded_fonts no))
